 he was  ultimately defeated by odin who banished  him to a prison realm known as the room  without doors  and so loki remained in the room without  doors for 60 years but would eventually  escape when one of his soldiers helmet  zemo  used the power of the nornstones to open  a gateway into the room which freed loki  now loki would continue to antagonize  his brother thor and the ultimates the  ultimate universe's version of the  avengers and tried to bring about world  war three  along with the liberators a team of  supervillains sponsored by several world  governments  and so after the ultimates defeated the  liberators loki tried to carry on the  mission of destroying the ultimates  himself and in doing so  summoned an army of monsters from asgard  but his plans were thwarted by odin who  sent asgardian warriors to repel the  attack  and also stripped loki of most of his  powers loki was then imprisoned by odin  once more but after he escaped he was  sent to hell by hella now somehow loki  either escapes or is freed from hell but  he dies in a siege of asgard by the  children of tomorrow a group of  superpower soldiers led by the maker the  ultimate universe's version of reed  richards and so not only does ultimate  loki's origin differ significantly from  the classic version but his powers do as  well although ultimate loki is a devious  trickster in much the same way that his  616 counterpart is his power set is far  beyond  anything that the main marvel universe  loki could ever hope to achieve  ultimate loki possesses superhuman  strength and has been able to harm his  brother  thor in a sparring session where he also  proved himself to be a capable fighter  he's skilled in a variety of weapons but  his weapon of choice is a bow and arrow  which he uses to slay multiple frost  giants  heimdall and balder loki also possesses  superhuman speed and durability and just  to get a sense of how durable he is he  survived beatings from thor  as well as surviving thor's lightning  attacks but what really sets loki apart  from the version that we're probably  more familiar with  is his reality warping ability this is  described as an ability to shuffle  time and space but in effect it's  basically just reality warping for  instance  on one occasion thor's in a restaurant  talking to volksdag about loki who thor  dismisses as not being a major threat  because every time they battle thor  always wins now volstagg tells thor  that this time is different and that  loki is moving the scenery around them  and rewriting reality itself  moments later a waiter comes up to thor  and says that the restaurant's other  patrons are concerned  because thor has been talking to himself  for five minutes thor is then taken  aback  and looks up to see that volstag is no  longer at the table and the waiter  confirms that he was never there at all  and so soon after this  loki creates a new persona for himself  taking the form of gunnar goldman who  claims to be part of the norwegian super  soldier program  and furthermore claims that thor is not  the god he claims to be but a product of  that super soldier program this of  course was a ruse designed to convince  the ultimates that thor is insane  and turn them against him but despite  thor's insistence that loki is  responsible for his ruse by shuffling  time and space the ultimates  indeed begin to question his sanity on  another occasion loki uses his reality  warping abilities to alter security tape  footage to make it appear that captain  america is responsible for the murder of  hawkeye's family when in reality  it was black widow who killed him now  loki is also able to bestow powers on  others as he did with valkyrie and the  rest of the ultimate defenders who in  turn  pledge their allegiance to loki loki's  capable of size manipulation of himself  and others  being able to either shrink to tiny  proportions or grow to massive ones he  can also create multiple copies of  himself  shapeshift and claims that he can alter  the color of the sun and the sky  he can teleport to anywhere he wants and  has displayed the ability to summon  various mythical creatures such as  serpents giants trolls and giant wolves  there are limitations to loki's power  though  as using them alerts odin to his  presence which loki tries to avoid at  all costs  as odin is capable of removing his  powers from him now it's also been  suggested that loki's powers are rooted  in sorcery  instead of outright reality warping as  his power has been shown to grow  and diminish at various points and so he  has been written somewhat inconsistently  and of course  any time he tangles with thor he usually  loses despite his reality warping  ability  because that's just how things work when  you fight four more often than not  but still ultimate loki has displayed  some incredibly  impressive feats and is vastly more  powerful than the 616 version  even counting the time that loki briefly  became the sorcerer supreme but even  still it's kind of surprising that loki  didn't do more with his powers than he  did because you would think he'd do some  crazy stuff or at least get a few more  victories and he did as most of his  plans ultimately ended up in failure but  that's the plight of super villains  they're always just being thwarted by  the good guys  but let me know what you guys think down  in the comments section if you guys are  new here to comments explain  make sure you guys hit the sub button to  become part of the rob core if you guys  enjoyed this video  make sure you drop a like and i will  catch you all later  [Music]  peace  [Music]  [Applause]  so  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  spectrum  [Applause]  [Music]  youtube  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  me  [Applause]  [Music]  you

